  "strategy": "Data lake was empty, so I downloaded public resources. (1) OmniPath enzsub (human, phosphorylation): 39,037 records aggregating PhosphoSitePlus, SIGNOR, HPRD, phospho.ELM, dbPTM, KEA, PhosphoNetworks, MIMP, ProtMapper (incl. text-mining sources REACH/Sparser/RLIMS-P), Li2012; collapsed to 39,015 kinase-substrate-site triplets with all source labels unioned. (2) SIGNOR human direct download: protein->protein phosphorylation rows with a residue; merged 9,704 matches and added 1,140 new triplets; skipped 1,513 rows lacking a parsable Ser/Thr/Tyr/His residue. Peptides are +/-3 windows from canonical UniProt sequences, kept only where the residue matched; otherwise SIGNOR's 15-mer was used. 3419 entries have no peptide because of residue/sequence mismatches; those entries are kept. Caveats: ProtMapper text-mining labels are lower-confidence; PhosphoSitePlus was only accessed through OmniPath, not directly.",
